<config xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="urn:magento:module:Magento_Config:etc/system_file.xsd">
    <system>
        <!-- Zero CMS's note on Page Builder's own setting (Setup\Patch\Data\TurnOffPageBuilder). -->
        <section id="cms">
            <group id="pagebuilder">
                <field id="enabled">
                    <comment><![CDATA[<strong>Zero CMS builds the pages of this store</strong> (Content &gt; Pages &gt; Edit with Zero CMS), so Page Builder is off. On the Zero storefront its sliders, tabs, carousels, video backgrounds and maps don't work, and its columns lose their layout: turn it on only for a store that doesn't use the Zero theme.]]></comment>
                </field>
            </group>
        </section>
        <section id="zero_cms" translate="label" type="text" sortOrder="15" showInDefault="1">
            <label>CMS</label>
            <tab>zero</tab>
            <resource>Zero_Cms::config</resource>
            <group id="ai" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="10" showInDefault="1">
                <label>AI</label>
                <comment>In the Zero CMS editor: build a page from a description, write, improve or shorten a text field, translate a page into the store view's language. Requests go from the server to the provider; the key never reaches the browser. Nothing is saved without a person: answers load into the editor as unsaved changes. Admin users also need the "Use AI" permission (Content > Elements > Zero CMS Editor).</comment>
                <field id="enabled" translate="label" type="select" sortOrder="10" showInDefault="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Enabled</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                </field>
                <field id="provider" translate="label" type="select" sortOrder="20" showInDefault="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Provider</label>
                    <source_model>Zero\Cms\Model\Config\Source\AiProvider</source_model>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="api_key" translate="label comment" type="obscure" sortOrder="30" showInDefault="1">
                    <label>Anthropic API Key</label>
                    <comment><![CDATA[From <a href="https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys" target="_blank" rel="noopener">console.anthropic.com</a>. Stored encrypted.]]></comment>
                    <backend_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Backend\Encrypted</backend_model>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                        <field id="provider">anthropic</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="model" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="40" showInDefault="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Model</label>
                    <comment>claude-opus-5-5 (best writing, default), claude-sonnet-5-5 (faster, cheaper), claude-haiku-4-5-20251001 (fastest).</comment>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                        <field id="provider">anthropic</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="bedrock_region" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="50" showInDefault="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Bedrock Region</label>
                    <comment>The AWS region Bedrock is called in, e.g. us-east-1 or eu-central-1. Claude's models must be enabled there (Bedrock > Model access).</comment>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                        <field id="provider">bedrock</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="bedrock_model" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="60" showInDefault="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Bedrock Model ID</label>
                    <comment>For the Zero CMS editor: a Bedrock model or inference profile id, e.g. us.anthropic.claude-haiku-4-5-20251001-v1:0 (Bedrock > Cross-region inference lists them). The AI Assistant has its own: Zero > AI Assistant.</comment>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                        <field id="provider">bedrock</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="bedrock_api_key" translate="label comment" type="obscure" sortOrder="70" showInDefault="1">
                    <label>Bedrock API Key (optional)</label>
                    <comment>Empty: the server's own AWS credentials (its EC2 role, allowed bedrock:InvokeModel), no key at all. Or a Bedrock API key from Bedrock > API keys. Stored encrypted.</comment>
                    <backend_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Backend\Encrypted</backend_model>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                        <field id="provider">bedrock</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
            </group>
        </section>
    </system>
</config>
